{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564495-requiem-promethean-homebrew-twin-cities","id":1564495,"title":"Requiem/Promethean Homebrew: Twin Cities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-02T18:00:00-07:00","id":1564495,"title":"Requiem/Promethean Homebrew: Twin Cities","content":"AI Summary of my personally written chronicle if anyone is interested or has thoughts...<br /> <br /> Chronicle Synthesis: The Architecture of the Twin Cities Workings<br /> ================================================== =================================<br /> METROPOLITAN MATRIX OVERVIEW<br /> ================================================== =================================<br /> \u2022 PHASE I: Mortal Infiltration &amp; The Ellsworth Folio<br /> \u2022 PHASE II: Geomantic Convergence &amp; Centimani Emergence (Pollyanna &amp; Varney)<br /> \u2022 PHASE III: The Hype Proliferation &amp; Municipal Uprising<br /> \u2022 PHASE IV: Awakening of the Primal Vein (Einar the Red &amp; The Ancient Elders)<br /> \u2022 PHASE V: Cross-River Schism (Hardwick's Highlands vs. The Sanctified Cross)<br /> \u2022 PHASE VI: The Heretical Alliance (The Lovers &amp; Bishop Sangris)<br /> \u2022 PHASE VII: The Zenith Catalyst (The Maw of the Unmade &amp; To Blot Out a Star)<br /> ================================================== =================================<br /> <br /> <b>Formula Result: </b> <hr />I. The Genesis of Geomantic Discovery: Mortals, the Promethean, and the FolioThe narrative architecture begins in the shadowy transit corridors of South Minneapolis, where a desperate cell of mortals\u2014operating on the fringes of municipal legality\u2014collided with a newly forged Promethean driven by the raw, agonizing spark of the Divine Fire. Drawn together by financial necessity, street-level survival, and an irresistible alchemical resonance, this fragile coterie uncovered the historic legacy of Simon Ellsworth.<br /> <br /> Ellsworth, a mid-century civic engineer who secretly embedded a fluid kinetic grid into the 1950s South Minneapolis streetcar lines, left behind a legacy at war with the heavy stone containment anchors of his rival, Richard Burgess. By recovering Ellsworth\u2019s lost Folio and deploying his micro-runed brass artifacts, the mortals and the Promethean learned that the city's street geometry was not a random product of urban expansion, but a carefully engineered occult centrifuge designed to harness kinetic friction and stabilize the subterranean bedrock. <hr />II. The Metaphysical Veil Lifts: Covenants, Grids, and the Centimani ThreatAs the cell delved deeper into Ellsworth\u2019s network, the thin veneer of mortal reality dissolved entirely. The party discovered that Minneapolis was carved into fiercely contested domain quadrants, ruled by ancient vampiric covenants who treated the city's street layout as a living mechanical engine. The 45-degree tilt of Downtown Minneapolis\u2014imposed by early Ventrue architects\u2014sheared violently against the compass grid of the outer neighborhoods, creating the volatile Nine-Sided Star (The Nonagram of Flux).<br /> <br /> This high-frequency geometric hum attracted dark, distorted forces from the alchemical fringes: the Centimani. Led by <b>Pollyanna</b>, a horrific, mutated flesh-sculptor haunting the Seward grain silos, and <b>Varney</b>, a sinister subterranean architect operating out of deep industrial battery zones, the Waster faction sought to hijack the Nonagram\u2019s current. Their objective was to overload the grid with toxic Flux, warping the city's spiritual current into an unholy nursery for Pandoran horrors. The mortals, stepping through the crucible of supernatural transformation, were forced to navigate the delicate balance between the Ordo Dracul\u2019s clinical, calcified stone batteries and the Circle of the Crone\u2019s wild, fluid blood-rituals. <hr />III. The Hype War Uprising: Alchemical Epidemic &amp; Street-Level UnrestThe cold war between the covenants erupted into open street warfare with the proliferation of <b>Hype</b>\u2014a highly volatile, alchemical narcotic infused with purified Vitae and Pyros residue. Manufactured in the industrial enclaves of the North Pasture under the authority of the Crescent Syndicate and distributed through subterranean hubs like Hype Depot B, Hype swept through the mortal nightlife of Lake Street, The Sprawl, and The Bone &amp; Bark.<br /> <br /> The drug acted as a chemical catalyst, inducing violent hallucinations, spontaneous frenzies, and acute psychic breaks among the mortal populace while corrupting the blood supply of local Kindred. Street gangs, unhoused youths, and rogue neonates clashed in the alleyways as the Invictus oligarchy sought to monetize the epidemic, while the Circle of the Crone weaponized the chaotic energy to disrupt corporate development over sacred nodes. The coterie found themselves trapped in the crossfire of this municipal uprising, tracing the supply lines from dark dance floors through stormwater culverts to the deep cisterns beneath the city. <hr />IV. Shadows of the Ancients: Einar the Red and the Pre-Metropolitan HeritageBeneath the modern conflict of neon and concrete lay an even older, deeper threat: the awakening of the Ancient Elders. Long before streetcar loops or glass skyscrapers were constructed, Viking Gangrel elders led by <b>Einar the Red Crow</b> crossed the Atlantic in the 14th century, driving cold-iron runespikes into the sandstone bluffs of the Upper Mississippi River Gorge to seal their sovereign claim over the &quot;Prime Vein&quot;.<br /> <br /> As modern infrastructure developments and high-voltage light rail lines inadvertently tapped into these dormant runic boundary gates, the sleeping elders began to stir from their centuries-long torpor. Operatives like H\u00e5kon Iron-Eye and the Unbound tracker Nistan, plagued by the disorienting <i>Fog of Ages</i>, began retrofitting modern industrial rail yards and electrical junction boxes to route municipal power directly toward Einar\u2019s subterranean tomb. The coterie realized that the modern court's political squabbles were built atop a volatile primeval foundation that threatened to erase the city's modern geometry entirely upon Einar's full resurgence. <hr />V. The Twin Cities Cold War: Prince Penn Hardwick vs. The Lancea SanctumDominating the metropolitan landscape was the century-long, architectural blood feud between <b>Prince Penn Hardwick</b>\u2014the cackling, eccentric Nosferatu/Ventrue-Malkavian sovereign of the Downtown Highlands\u2014and the fanatical <b>Lancea Sanctum</b> of St. Paul, led by Cardinal Salazar and Grand Paladin Judith.<br /> <br /> Penn viewed Minneapolis as a pristine clockwork board game, utilizing his network of skyways, digital taps, and hidden city cameras to insulate his glass tower fortress. Across the Mississippi River, the Sanctum locked down St. Paul using the <b>Perfect Cross</b>\u2014a rigid, cruciform network anchored by the Cathedral of St. Paul, designed to freeze spiritual energy and suppress free-willed Kindred. Penn\u2019s covert 1915 assassination of Sanctum holy figures had anchored the eastern points of the Nine-Sided Star, locking St. Paul out of Minneapolis. However, as the Hype War destabilized the border checkpoints along the river bridges, young Sanctified zealots pushed for a formal Dispensation of Incursion to invade the Highlands and purge Penn\u2019s secular court. <hr />VI. The Heretical Alliance: The Lovers and Bishop SangrisAs Prince Penn\u2019s paranoia escalated, an unprecedented, dangerous alliance was forged across covenant and domain lines. <b>The Lovers</b> (Julian and Soren), the blood-obsessed Hierophants of the Circle of the Crone in South Minneapolis, established a secret pact with <b>Bishop Sangris</b>, the bloodstained &quot;Crimson Hammer&quot; commanding the subterranean axis of the Lancea Sanctum.<br /> <br /> Though philosophically opposed, both factions shared a single objective: the absolute dismantling of Prince Penn\u2019s clockwork reign. Recognizing that the Iron Cradle Lock kept Penn\u2019s pristine glass Highlands anchored, The Lovers channeled corrupted Vitae into Node 07 (The Midtown Greenway Trench) while Sangris manipulated the eastern riverbed anchors. Their goal was not to release the Maw of the Unmade entirely, but to &quot;loosen the bolts&quot; just enough to cause a localized structural collapse under downtown Minneapolis. By warping the cross-river geometry, they sought to snap the lead-soldered bands of Penn's grid, causing his Highlands core to sink into the subterranean bedrock and shattering his political power forever. <hr />VII. The Zenith Catalyst: The Maw of the Unmade &amp; To Blot Out a StarThe chronicle reaches its apocalyptic climax as all converging vectors\u2014the Ellsworth and Burgess grids, the Centimani Flux, the Hype War, and the heretical alliance between the Coven and the Sanctum\u2014threaten the ultimate containment seal: <b>The Iron Cradle Lock</b>.<br /> <br /> Miles beneath the limestone cellars of the Twin Cities lies <b>The Maw of the Unmade</b>, a vast, pressurized subterranean vault holding thousands of calcified, pre-glacial Pandorans. The opposing surface geometries\u2014Minneapolis\u2019s kinetic Nine-Sided Star and St. Paul\u2019s static Perfect Cross\u2014functioned as a massive, metaphysical vise grip that kept the Maw frozen in slumber.<br /> <br /> In the final arc, <i>To Blot Out a Star</i>, the calculated sabotage by The Lovers and Bishop Sangris backfires. Rather than merely undermining Penn\u2019s downtown fortress, the structural damage causes the lead-soldered iron bands of the Lock to snap completely. As localized gravity anomalies, Gutter-Spark infestations, and violent Flux surges erupt across South Minneapolis, Prince Penn Hardwick, the Coven mages, and the Ordo Dracul scholars scramble to manipulate the coterie. The party is thrust into the ultimate decision: act as grease-monkeys to tighten the structural bolts of a usurped, mad Prince\u2019s engine, or allow the Nine-Sided Star to shatter completely\u2014shattering the Twin Cities' metaphysical balance and unsealing the cosmic nightmare waiting beneath the frost line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29184-pennhardwick","name":"PennHardwick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T19:01:17-07:00","id":1564624,"title":"","content":"I wish I cracked my Promie book open a bit more. As for the vamps, you don't get to live another 50-years to get your BP up a dot by fighting other supernatural-beings that could bring Final-Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}